; Caulder, the full theme from sketch D1 "Claw, low": B minor, 124 bpm, a 2-bar intro and a 32-bar loop (about 62 s). Low strings carry a leaping hook over a pick-bass gallop, horn stabs and a four-on-the-floor kit with claps (A); the hook goes a fourth up through E minor and C and sinks to F# (B); a horn sings a proud tune in D major over a half-time stomp and a dark pad (C); the hook returns with a low horn answering in the gaps (A2).
; Strings A.48, horn A.111, pick bass A.36, kit A.120, timpani A.47, pad A.26. Original notes, AW2 voices, no rom lines.
song caulder
tempo 124
meter 4/4
reverb 173
priority 0

inst str = A.48 shift=0
inst horn = A.111 shift=-12
inst pick = A.36 shift=24
inst kit = A.120
inst timp = A.47 shift=24
inst pad = A.26 shift=0
inst low = A.111 shift=-12
hit kick=36 rim=37 clap=39 snare=40 hat=44 ohat=46 tom1=45 tom2=48 tom3=50 crash=49

